            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CAL01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Vicomte</roleName>
                        <forename>Charles Alexander</forename>
                        <surname>Calonne</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1734">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1802"/>
                    <occupation>French statesman</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Calonne was appointed Controller-General of Finances for France in 1783 but was subsequently blamed for France's enormous fiscal problems and dismissed. He then 
    moved to England in 1787.</p>
                        <p>Besides his death, Godwin recorded two meetings, both in 1794. 
  Calonne lived in London for much of the 1790s - a note in the <title>Garden 
  History Society</title> for 1799 refers to Calonne buying Wimbledon House
  and gardens from Bond Hopkins in 1791. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="journalism"> Michael Symes, 'Benjamin Bond Hopkins at Painshill', <title>Garden History</title> 
    27.2 (Winter 1999), p. 239-243.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
